  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The minimum number of elements that must be added to relation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;on the set&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, so that it is an equivalence relation is</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "13",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>}</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>A</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><strong>Reflexive:</strong></p><p>For reflexivity, we must add&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><strong>Symmetric and Transitive:</strong></p><p>For symmetric and transitivity, we must add</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So, we can say that minimum&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn></math>&nbsp;elements are required to make an equivalence relation.</p>",
